/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * OFFICIAL PUBLISHED FIGURES — the only real data in this platform.
 *
 * Everything else the app renders is generated by a seeded PRNG (see
 * mockData.js). The figures in THIS file are not. Each one was read from a
 * government publication on the date recorded in `retrievedOn`, and carries
 * the publisher, the source URL, and the exact period it covers.
 *
 * RULES FOR THIS FILE — they are the whole point of it:
 *
 *   1. Never add a figure without a source URL that states it. If a number
 *      cannot be traced to a publication, it belongs in mockData.js, not here.
 *   2. Never restate a figure for a period other than the one it was published
 *      for. `period` and `asAt` are not decoration — an officer reading
 *      "10,11,501 dealers" needs to know that is April 2025, not today.
 *   3. These are point-in-time captures, NOT a live feed. The app makes no
 *      network calls. When a source publishes a newer figure, this file has to
 *      be edited by hand — `retrievedOn` is what tells a reader how stale it is.
 *   4. Where a source could not be read programmatically, it is listed under
 *      DATASET_POINTERS with no value attached. An unread source gets a link,
 *      never a guess.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

